  "about": "'Prepared By Client List' from the National American Indian Housing Council's IFM training manual, section 8: the items 'included in a typical PBC list for a client with a December 31 year-end', dated for 2018. Pages 1-3 of the PDF, copied unchanged; page 3 goes on into SEFA guidance with its own 1) and a. lists, which are not requests and should not be read as any. Twelve numbered sections ('1. Planning:') with lettered items a), b), ...; the section lines are headings, the 33 lettered items are the requests, refs written as 1.a. Period FY2018 throughout except 4.c (deposits Jan-Mar 2019) and two that run to the fieldwork date and so have no end date: 1.c (minutes for the year 'through the scheduled date of the fieldwork') and 7.b (checks written from 12/31/2018 on). Balance requests 'as of December 31, 2018' use the fiscal year, as elsewhere in the corpus; a reader could fairly take them as the single day. 11.a reconciles FY2017's net position to FY2018's and is scored FY2018. 2.b asks for 'January 31, 2018 bank statements', probably meaning 2019; scored as FY2018. Ramp-answerable: only 7.b, a subsequent-disbursements listing (bill_support). 7.a (AP listing at year end with open invoices) is an aging report, 5.a (prepaid schedule with invoices) and 6.a (capital assets with invoices) are outside Ramp even though they mention invoices. No dollar thresholds.",
